// ugui/ui_context.{h,cc}: UIContext, which owns every subsystem and drives a
// frame: input, timers, animations, measure, layout, paint, tooltip,
// overlays; UIConfig, FrameReuse, FrameStats.
//
// Shape differences (not behavior):
//
// * UIContext<P: Platform, R: Rhi, S: ScriptRuntime> is generic over the
//   three link-time seams (PORTING.md, "Seams"); the defaults are the host
//   platform, NullRhi and NoScript.
// * Init takes the UIConfig by value. A C++ draw-data Init without an
//   external window fails unless ULTRAGUI_PLATFORM_HOST; here unless the
//   platform says it is host-fed (`Platform::host_fed`).
// * There is no widget context member pointing at the subsystems: every call
//   into widget code builds a WidgetContext from views of this struct's
//   fields (text engine, animator, platform, the clock, the default font and
//   ui scale) and lends it beside the World, the way the C++'s widget_ctx_
//   is read. `ui_scale()` is that member's ui_scale.
// * The texture seam: draw-data mode keeps the host's TextureBackendBox in
//   the renderer (Renderer2D owns it, `texture_backend()` lends it); legacy
//   mode routes textures through the Rhi (the C++ RHITextureBackend), which
//   the renderer resolves in end_frame and LoadSvg/LoadAnim reach through an
//   RhiTextureBackend built per call.
// * LoadAnim returns an AnimId (an index; animations live until Shutdown, as
//   in the C++) and `anim(id)`/`anim_var(id)` resolve it; the C++ hands out
//   the VectorAnimation*.
// * LoadLottie/LoadVideo live in their packages (the core cannot import
//   them). Their players reach UIContext through frame extensions: a
//   `UiExtension` (see below) added with `add_extension` is updated where the
//   C++ updates lottie_anims_ and video_players_, asked for NeedsConvert /
//   ConvertFrame where the C++ asks the video players, and shut down where
//   the C++ deletes them.
// * The script runtime's hooks into UIContext (the C++ Init registers
//   RegisterAnimLua & co. with lambdas capturing `this`): `script_host()`
//   lends a ScriptHost (anim loading, widget lookup by name, extensions)
//   beside the World and the WidgetContext, see ScriptHost.
// * The audio backend is an owned AudioBackendBox (`set_audio(box)`), silent
//   by default; UIContext inits and shuts it down as the C++ does.
// * PaintCallback is `own fn(&var Renderer2D, &var R): ()`.
// * The animator's apply/done callbacks are collected and applied after
//   Animator::update returns (a closure cannot lend the World twice); they
//   only write the widgets' animation styles, in the same order.

module ultragui::ui_context;

